From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] ole32: direct single-writer storage, MoveElementTo, element times (6006)

Structured storage left the direct single-writer mode's IDirectWriterLock,
IStorage::MoveElementTo and SetElementTimes as stubs (COM-STORAGE).

StgCreateDocfile accepts STGM_DIRECT_SWMR | STGM_READWRITE |
STGM_SHARE_DENY_WRITE (ole32 storage32 test_direct_swmr runs on Windows:
its todo_wine is removed), and a storage created that way is a writer too.
IDirectWriterLock: WaitForWriteAccess locks a byte of the file's lock range
(waiting up to the timeout, STG_E_INUSE after it), ReleaseWriteAccess
unlocks it (STG_E_ACCESSDENIED without access), HaveWriteAccess says which.
MoveElementTo copies a stream or a storage under the new name (replacing one
there) and, with STGMOVE_MOVE, destroys the original. SetElementTimes writes
the creation and modification times into the directory entry (no name: the
storage itself), and Stat reports them. A compound file stream's
LockRegion/UnlockRegion return STG_E_INVALIDFUNCTION, as documented; the
internal storages' Revert (direct mode: no effect) and STGM_NOSCRATCH
(the scratch is in memory) no longer warn.
---
 dlls/ole32/stg_stream.c      |  10 ++-
 dlls/ole32/storage32.c       | 174 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++-------
 dlls/ole32/storage32.h       |   5 ++
 dlls/ole32/tests/storage32.c |   1 -
 4 files changed, 158 insertions(+), 32 deletions(-)

